-- Generated by tools/build_manual.py; edit docs/manual/book.json.
return [====[ic, but become Reckless for 30 seconds: your attacks can harm allies.</td></tr><tr><td>Contraband Countdown</td><td>One shared item. Its price falls while you wait; another Hero can buy it first.</td></tr><tr><td>Life Underwriter</td><td>Sell one reserve life for 40 $DEB. Your final life cannot be sold.</td></tr></table><p>Press Use to review the exact offer. Press Use again within 12 seconds to confirm it. If your inventory, Hero or offer changes, review the refreshed offer before paying. Looking at a machine does not buy anything.</p><p>Each account gets one successful transaction per service per dungeon, except Contraband Countdown, whose one lot goes to the first buyer. Starter and DFT equipment cannot be salvaged or reforged. Insufficient resources, full bags or full stacks leave payment untouched.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 98</div></article><article class="page" id="prison-incidents" data-title="Read the room"><div class="kicker">Dungeon Events</div><h2>Read the room</h2><table><tr><td>Steam Vent</td><td>Four seconds safe, one second warning, one second steam. Within 64 units, a failed WIS save can Mute you for 2 seconds. Seal the valve or walk around.</td></tr><tr><td>Stasis Beacon</td><td>Standing close risks 2 seconds of Clumsy after a failed DEX save. Crouch past it or switch it off.</td></tr><tr><td>Watchful Eye</td><td>Meeting its gaze risks 3 seconds of Reckless after a failed WIS save. Avert your eyes, circle behind the screen and unplug it.</td></tr><tr><td>Prison Surveyor</td><td>Ask for your current objective’s physical floor and first steps along the presently open route.</td></tr><tr><td>Silent Archive</td><td>Use, then stay grounded, motionless and quiet for 4 seconds to restore up to 25 Magic. Moving cancels freely.</td></tr></table><p>The three machines impose ordinary saving throws and existing conditions. Their effects are avoidable; disabling a machine makes it safe for everyone. A disabled machine grants no cash reward. Normal combat continues while you investigate.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 99</div></article><article class="page" id="prison-challenges" data-title="The prison plays games"><div class="kicker">Dungeon Events</div><h2>The prison plays games</h2><table><tr><td>Counterweight Cache</td><td>Two Heroes hold opposite plates for 3 seconds. Alone, use the central lever and hold still for 10 seconds. Once open, each account collects 15 $DEB.</td></tr><tr><td>Prison Relay</td><td>Run across numbered markers 1, 2 and 3 in order within 12 seconds, then collect 15 $DEB at the console.</td></tr><tr><td>Memory Terminal</td><td>Watch three numbered lights, then use the corresponding buttons in order for 15 $DEB. You have 30 seconds; mistakes let you try again without charge.</td></tr><tr><td>Nerve Clock</td><td>Use to start, then use again during green for 20 $DEB. Red spends your attempt and risks 3 seconds of Reckless. The cycle is 3 seconds red, 1 green.</td></tr><tr><td>Strength Press</td><td>One non-exploding d20 plus your STR modifier against 12. Success pays 20 $DEB; failure spends the attempt without charging you.</td></tr></table><p>Numbered markers and personal prompts show the current challenge. Each successful reward belongs to your account once per dungeon; other Heroes have their own claims. Nerve Clock and Strength Press also remember unsuccessful results.</p><p>These games do not pause the dungeon or protect you from enemies. Let a friend watch the corridor. Counterweight’s solo lever means every challenge remains usable without a second human.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 100</div></article><article class="page" id="locked-chest" data-title="A key, or a Rogue’s touch"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>A key, or a Rogue’s touch</h2><table><tr><td>Chest Key</td><td>Bag-only consumable; stacks up to nine. Press E at a locked chest to use one.</td></tr><tr><td>Rogue lockpick</td><td>Press E without a key, or hold Sprint + E to pick while carrying keys.</td></tr><tr><td>Success chance</td><td>5% per Combat Level, up to 95%; one ordinary d100 roll.</td></tr></table><p>The locked loot chest sits off the required rescue route and offers each Steam account one ordinary procedural wearable per dungeon. It does not award a DFT; the item uses your normal equipment storage.</p><p>Chest Keys can appear among normal loot drops and remain in your bag rather than the Throwable slot. A key is spent only when its chest item successfully enters your equipment storage. A full bag or failed delivery spends no key; make room or retry.</p><p>A Rogue gets one lockpick attempt per chest. Failure uses that attempt but leaves any key intact, and you may later open the chest with a key. A full bag or another rejected preflight does not use the attempt. If a successful pick cannot deliver the item, retry to claim the same reward without another roll or a key.</p><p>The chest remembers your account’s claim and lockpick attempt through reconnects, replacement Heroes, and regeneration of the same dungeon. Those actions cannot grant another attempt or reroll the reward. A new dungeon provides a new opportunity; a new campaign resets the chest record.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 101</div></article><article class="page" id="treasure-chest" data-title="Treasure to keep"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Treasure to keep</h2><table><tr><td>DFT treasure event</td><td>One ordinary d2 selects one or two optional chests; each chest offers each Steam account one DFT.</td></tr><tr><td>Collection capacity</td><td>Eight DFTs. Ordinary equipment bag space does not limit this reward.</td></tr><tr><td>Opening the lock</td><td>Use a Chest Key, or use the same Rogue lockpicking controls and chance as an ordinary locked chest.</td></tr></table><p>Treasure chests hold persistent Debbie Fund Tokens, not ordinary equipment pickups. Each Hero has an independent claim at each chest. The reward is fixed: reconnecting, replacing your Hero, or regenerating the same dungeon cannot reroll it or restore a claim. Selling or recreating the awarded DFT does not reopen the chest.</p><p>Press E to spend one Chest Key when the DFT is successfully delivered. A Rogue without a key may pick the lock; hold Sprint + E to choose lockpicking while carrying keys. Each account gets one attempt per chest at 5% per Combat Level, up to 95%. A failed pick consumes the attempt but no key; you can return with a key.</p><p>A full DFT collection spends neither key nor lockpick attempt. Make room in your collection, then return. A storage failure spends no key. If a successful pick cannot deliver its DFT, the chest stays unlocked for your account: retry for the same reward without another roll or key.</p><p>Treasure events appear only on a four-event selection and contain one or two optional chests. Their DFTs persist in your server-local collection and have no cash value. Leaving the dungeon ends access to its chests. For an administrator preview, use lod_event_preview_generate treasure_chest; lod_chest_key_testkit supplies one key only if you have none.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 102</div></article><article class="page" id="vending-machine" data-title="A bottle for the road"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>A bottle for the road</h2><table><tr><td>Healing Potion · $10 DEB</td><td>One bottle per Steam account per campaign dungeon. Each Hero has an independent purchase.</td></tr><tr><td>Potion effect</td><td>Restores 25 HP and cures negative statuses when used. Buying the bottle does not heal you.</td></tr><tr><td>Carrying capacity</td><td>Healing Potions stack up to three and use the Throwable slot.</td></tr></table><p>Press E at a vending machine to buy one standard Healing Potion for your equipment inventory. The price uses your persistent, server-local $DEB balance, which has no cash value. The potion is ordinary run equipment, not a DFT.</p><p>Insufficient funds, a full potion stack, a storage failure, or leaving the interaction before it can complete spends nothing and leaves your purchase available. Correct the problem and retry. A successful purchase charges exactly $10 DEB and delivers one bottle.</p><p>The machine remembers your account’s completed purchase through death, replacement Heroes, reconnects, and regeneration of the same dungeon. Drinking or discarding the bottle does not restock the machine, and reconnecting does not replace a lost bottle. A new dungeon or campaign provides a new purchase.</p><p>This optional machine can appear alongside other Dungeon Events. For an administrator preview, use lod_event_preview_generate vending_machine. Purchases spend real server-local $DEB; the preview does not provide free currency.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 103</div></article><article class="page" id="false-floor" data-title="Watch your step"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Watch your step</h2><p>A False-floor hazard is a small panel in an optional upper-floor room. Stepping fully onto it as a grounded Hero can open the floor beneath you. There is no E prompt to activate it. The solid rim around the panel gives you room to go around.</p><p>The fall leads one floor down. Ordinary gravity and falling consequences apply. The destination preserves your current progression access, and the existing stairs provide a route back; the trap never opens a locked progression shortcut.</p><p>The panel stays open for at least three seconds. It closes and rearms only after its opening is clear, so keep moving after landing. All Heroes share the same panel state, and the hazard can trigger again. If the landing is unsafe or occupied before activation, the panel stays closed.</p><p>For an administrator preview, use lod_event_preview_generate false_floor. Redeploy after generation and follow the printed locator.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 104</div></article><article class="page" id="warp-hole" data-title="A shorter way back"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>A shorter way back</h2><p>From Dungeon Level 5 onward, a paired warp hole may appear as an optional event. Its two cyan endpoints sit on different physical floors. The prompt identifies your endpoint and its destination floor.</p><p>Press E at either dormant endpoint. Your first successful traversal links the pair for everyone until this dungeon ends. Linked holes are free and repeatable; wait one second between your own traversals. Other Heroes can use them independently.</p><p>A warp hole shortens a route you can already reach. It never skips a locked gate, required boss, key or rescue step, and the ordinary stairs still provide a way back. It preserves your facing and stops your previous momentum.</p><p>If the arrival is occupied or unsafe, you stay where you are. Clear the landing and try again. A refused first traversal leaves the pair dormant. Regeneration replaces both endpoints with a fresh dormant pair.</p><p>For an administrator preview, use lod_event_preview_generate warp_hole. This unranked single-event preview can show the pair before Dungeon Level 5. Redeploy after generation and follow the printed locators.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 105</div></article><article class="page" id="tips" data-title="Deborah&#x27;s parting advice"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Deborah&#x27;s parting advice</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Deborah demonstrates" class="art" style="background-size:300% 200%;background-position:50% 100%"></div><ol><li>The clock pauses in staging and starts when the first Hero deploys. Every new dungeon gives you thirty minutes.</li><li>Keep a useful spell selected. A bottle in your hand means you are holding a bottle—not casting.</li><li>Move sideways out of committed charges. A longer corridor is not always a safer escape.</li><li>Compare gear drawbacks as carefully as benefits. Keep your permanent feat requirements in mind.</li><li>Use short map checks, read the current objective, and remember the stairs.</li><li>When the current boss falls, finish the job. At Level 20, defeat Hector after Gordon. Then Jail Key, jail door, rescue target.</li></ol><blockquote>“You&#x27;ve read the book. Now make yourself useful.”<br>— Deborah</blockquote><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 106</div></article><article class="page" id="skeleton-blockade" data-title="Skeleton of a Hero"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Skeleton of a Hero</h2><table><tr><td>Class</td><td>Fighter, Rogue or Wizard, chosen when the dungeon is built.</td></tr><tr><td>Combat Level</td><td>Dungeon Level + 2, capped at 20.</td></tr><tr><td>Passage</td><td>Defeat the Skeleton once; the route opens for everyone.</td></tr></table><p>Skeleton Blockades are frequent encounters from Dungeon Level 1. After two completed dungeons with events but no Skeleton, the next event selection includes one. The other event slots and rare-event rules still apply.</p><p>A Skeleton of a Hero guards a required passage. Its name begins “Skeleton of” and comes from the same name generator as your Hero. Its abilities, identity perks, class growth, health dice and eligible automatic feats use the ordinary Hero framework, with AI choices restricted to abilities its controller can use.</p><p>The Fighter closes in for melee, the Rogue fires SMG bursts, and the Wizard warns before striking a ground arc. Wizard arcs spend 12 base Magic plus their Content cost, modified by ordinary offensive Magic rules. Wizards cycle their generated Contents and must regenerate when their Magic runs low. Shared defenses, status effects and class rules still apply.</p><p>The Skeleton is always on the approachable side of its barrier. Fight it before crossing. A legitimate defeat opens the tall barrier for every Hero, including later arrivals; your normal keycard, boss and rescue sequence remains intact. Regenerating the dungeon creates a fresh encounter.</p><p>Combat XP follows ordinary killing-blow and damage-contribution rules, and normal individualized enemy drops apply. There is no extra cash, DFT or guaranteed equipment award. Removing the enemy is not a combat victory.</p><p>Administrator preview: lod_event_preview_generate skeleton_blockade. Redeploy and follow the printed location. The preview is unranked.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 107</div></article><article class="page" id="fallen-heroes" data-title="Your bones remember"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Your bones remember</h2><table><tr><td>When a player dies</td><td>Their build returns as an enemy AI skeleton.</td></tr><tr><td>Before it attacks</td><td>Three seconds of rattling bones and a violet warning.</td></tr><tr><td>After respawning</td><td>Your skeleton is still out there. Protect each other.</td></tr></table><p>A death in the active dungeon leaves a named skeleton near the fallen player. This happens even when dungeon events are switched off. It copies the identity, class, level, abilities, feats, equipment, weapons and remaining resources of the body that died, and rises at full copied maximum health. A fallen player-controlled Soldier copies that Soldier incarnation.</p><p>The skeleton uses its copied weapons and spells against the Heroes. Firearms spend copied ammunition; Wands spend copied charges; spells spend and regenerate Magic. A copied Soldier retains the Soldier rifle’s unlimited ammunition. Wall and Summon spells belong to the enemy side too. Red attack warnings give you time to react.</p><p>These are independent copies. Changing gear, respawning or disconnecting cannot weaken or erase them. Their duplicated gear cannot be looted, and defeating them awards no experience or other kill rewards. Ordinary event Skeletons still have their normal combat rewards.</p><p>Defeat your own skeleton to lay your bones to rest, or avenge a teammate. Staging deaths and deaths after dungeon completion create no skeleton. All remaining copies clear when the dungeon ends. If a death site is blocked, the skeleton waits for a safe nearby place to rise.</p><blockquote>“Keep your friends alive. You already know how dangerous their builds are.”<br>— Deborah</blockquote><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 108</div></article><article class="page" id="equipment-quiz" data-title="The Game Master: know what you wear"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>The Game Master: know what you wear</h2><table><tr><td>Before accepting</td><td>One attempt per account per dungeon. Decline freely.</td></tr><tr><td>Correct answer</td><td>One DFT, only when collection succeeds.</td></tr><tr><td>Wrong answer</td><td>The real worn item is stolen.</td></tr><tr><td>Time limit</td><td>30 seconds after acceptance; the dungeon keeps running.</td></tr></table><p>A suspiciously familiar grin waits in an optional hidden alcove. Press E at the Game Master and read his offer. You have 30 seconds to accept. Your task is to identify one piece of equipment you are wearing among two plausible phonies. The three cards show names, slots and properties. You cannot consult Equipment, Character Sheet, Wallet or the other Player Menu pages while answering.</p><p>Only ordinary procedural wearables are at risk. Weapons, consumables, protected or bound gear, free starting items and DFT-created equipment are excluded. Paired gloves count as one item and occupy both hands. No eligible equipment, a full eight-token DFT collection or unavailable reward storage means no accepted attempt.</p><p>Answer within 30 seconds. A wrong submitted answer removes the selected real item and its equipment effects. Cancelling, closing, timing out, dying, disconnecting, moving out of range or line of sight, or losing the current challenge forfeits the attempt without theft or reward. The world does not pause or protect you.</p><p>A correct answer earns one persistent, server-local DFT with no cash value. If storage fails after your answer, the result reads pending rather than success. Your menus reopen; use the same Game Master to retry the same frozen reward while the same Hero life, worn item and dungeon remain valid. Losing that binding forfeits an uncollected reward.</p><p>The Game Master disappears for you after your attempt ends. Other Heroes retain their own independent attempt and may play simultaneously. Reconnecting, changing Heroes or regenerating this dungeon does not grant another attempt. A new dungeon does. Late arrivals see the encounter appropriate to their own account.</p><p>Administrator preview: lod_event_preview_generate equipment_quiz. Redeploy with eligible ordinary wearable equipment and follow the printed locator. The preview is unranked but confirmed play risks actual equipment and awards a persistent DFT.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 109</div></article><article class="page" id="encounter-ecology" data-title="The prison changes its company"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>The prison changes its company</h2><p>Each dungeon draws its ordinary encounter squads from a tactical theme: Hunting Grounds, Occupation, Corruption, Crossfire, Quarantine or Funeral Retinue. Hunters pursue and ambush; occupation mixes guards and enforcers; corruption brings strange attacks; crossfire fills firing lanes; quarantine controls space; funeral retinues pair specialists with allies.</p><p>The prison avoids its two most recent themes and favors unfamiliar squads. Directed encounters draw from a themed selection, while roaming monsters use a much broader shared cast with extra weight for the dungeon’s favored types. A theme is not a promise that every wandering enemy will be the same few kinds. Keycard guards keep their own authored rules.</p><p>Roaming populations also change with the dungeon: Corruption favors Deadcrabs and Bio Blasters, Crossfire favors ranged bodies, Hunting Grounds favors Runners, Occupation favors Soldiers, and Funeral Retinue favors Shamblers. A few independent specialists can join them: Siphoners, Caromers, Reapers, Redliners, Drubbers and Afterbursts. Support teams, linked pairs, fixed traps and bosses remain in authored encounters. Roamers travel alone; their presence is not a promise of an escort.</p><p>Hunting Grounds and Occupation aim for twenty living roamers per physical floor; other themes aim for eighteen. The prison never budgets more than sixty-four roamers in total, so four-floor dungeons aim for sixteen per floor. Up to eight roamers on a floor may be distinct specialists, without duplicate living roaming specialists of one kind. A dead monster’s vacancy gets an opportunity about every twenty seconds, and some themes leave it empty longer. Initial positions that could not be filled retry separately, without replaying missed spawns. New bodies need clear supported homes away from Heroes and protected objectives, plus a usable patrol exit; full or obstructed areas wait rather than force a spawn.</p><p>The shape of the prison influences which squads fit: ambushers favor corners, pursuit units favor alternate routes, and firing teams favor clear straight approaches. Vertical approaches can attract Climbers; junctions and approaches to keycards can favor support squads. These are tendencies, not guarantees. Ordinary encounter groups leave space between their home positions, though wandering or pursuing enemies can still converge.</p><p>Sectors have a rhythm along the route from their entrance toward the keycard or the approachable side of the Black Gate: brief quiet stretches, lighter probes, pressure and a short recovery approach. Ordinary fights and patrol homes favor the routes you traverse, while deeper branches retain surprises. Entrance and goal respite bands are short, not whole empty regions. Hunting Grounds favors ambush phrases, Occupation and Crossfire pressure, and Funeral Retinue surges or ambushes; every rhythm remains possible. Probes keep their characteristic enemies and companions, with fewer extra bodies as party size and dungeon level grow. Keycard fights retain their own rules. Beyond the protected dungeon opening, wandering, pursuit, backtracking and separated teammates can still interrupt ordinary sector respite. The entrance sanctuary and its shared opening-pressure limit remain separate protections.</p><p>A theme changes how often enemies can arrive, and therefore your opportunity to meet an Elite; it does not change an individual enemy’s tier roll. Every ordinary body still rolls 60% Typical, 30% Elite or 10% Champion. Tells, weaknesses, rewards and abilities keep their own rules. Read each encounter: companions, cover and escape routes still matter. A new campaign starts a new encounter history.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 110</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_academic_achievement" data-title="Academic Achievement"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Academic Achievement</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_ACADEMIC_ACHIEVEMENT"><h3>Academic Achievement</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / magic_pool</p><p>Add your positive CHA modifier to your INT modifier when calculating passive Magic regeneration. Regeneration must be permitted.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 111</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_aggressive_personality" data-title="Aggressive Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Aggressive Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_AGGRESSIVE_PERSONALITY"><h3>Aggressive Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / eligible physical attack</p><p>Your next eligible attributable physical attack adds your positive CHA modifier as damage. No range requirement: legal distant attacks qualify too. Cooldown: one sealed, non-exploding 1d3-second roll.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 112</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_aura_burst" data-title="Aura Burst"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Aura Burst</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_AURA_BURST_1"><h3>Aura Burst</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage within radius 1 cells: a 3x3 same-floor neighborhood. Sustained drain does not trigger it.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_RADIANCE_2"><h3>Radiance</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Aura Burst</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage within radius 2 cells: a 5x5 same-floor neighborhood. Sustained drain does not trigger it. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MAJESTY_3"><h3>Majesty</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Radiance</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage within radius 3 cells: a 7x7 same-floor neighborhood. Sustained drain does not trigger it. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 113</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_hitstun_presence" data-title="Unnerving Presence"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Unnerving Presence</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_1"><h3>Unnerving Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 100% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_2"><h3>Dazing Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Unnerving Presence</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 200% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_3"><h3>Overwhelming Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dazing Presence</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 300% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 114</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_intimidation_proc" data-title="Daunting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Daunting</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_1"><h3>Daunting</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 55% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_2"><h3>Cowing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Daunting</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 75% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_3"><h3>Overawing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Cowing</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 95% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 115</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_menace" data-title="Menacing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Menacing</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_1"><h3>Menacing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Gain +2 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 30% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_2"><h3>Dreadful</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Menacing</p><p>Gain +4 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 25% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_3"><h3>Terrifying</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>Gain +4 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 20% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot. Each target’s first Morale save against you per encounter rolls twice and keeps the lower die. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 116</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_panic" data-title="Panic Is Contagious"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Panic Is Contagious</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_PANIC"><h3>Panic Is Contagious</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>When an enemy fails Morale against you, AI enemies below half HP within 2 connected cells make a Morale check. This cannot cascade again; each target is immune to cascades for 3 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 117</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_personality_aura" data-title="Abrasive Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Abrasive Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_ABRASIVE_PERSONALITY_1"><h3>Abrasive Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Every 3 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage within radius 1 cells: a 3x3 same-floor neighborhood. Wait the full initial interval; no catch-up pulses.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_NARCISSISM_2"><h3>Narcissism</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Abrasive Personality</p><p>Every 3 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage within radius 2 cells: a 5x5 same-floor neighborhood. Wait the full initial interval; no catch-up pulses. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MEGALOMANIA_3"><h3>Megalomania</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Narcissism</p><p>Every 3 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage within radius 3 cells: a 7x7 same-floor neighborhood. Wait the full initial interval; no catch-up pulses. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 118</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_self_actualization" data-title="Self-Actualization"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Self-Actualization</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_SELF_ACTUALIZATION"><h3>Self-Actualization</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / eligible Magic Form</p><p>Add your positive CHA modifier to each target’s magical damage, once after damage multipliers.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 119</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_winning_personality" data-title="Winning Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Winning Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_WINNING_PERSONALITY"><h3>Winning Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17</p><p>Gain +1 intrinsic CHA, up to the ability ceiling. Use the higher of INT or CHA to meet INT feat ability requirements. Other prerequisites still apply.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 120</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_big_guy" data-title="Big Guy"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Big Guy</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BIG_GUY"><h3>Big Guy</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 and STR 13</p><p>Your body and hurt volume become 30% larger. Gain 15% melee reach and 20% physical push dealt. Your movement hull stays the same. Incompatible with Little Guy.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 121</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_blast_proof" data-title="Blast-Proof"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Blast-Proof</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BLAST_PROOF"><h3>Blast-Proof</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Stop the first continuation of an incoming exploding damage chain. Keep damage already rolled; other chains continue normally. Cooldown: 2 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 122</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_glow_up" data-title="Glow Up"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Glow Up</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_GLOW_UP"><h3>Glow Up</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires a usable explicit CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p><p>Whenever your own ability adds your positive CHA modifier as damage, also add your positive CON modifier once to that damage event.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an authored CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 123</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_health_regeneration" data-title="Second Wind"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Second Wind</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_11"><h3>Second Wind</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 22% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_22"><h3>Rapid Recovery</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Second Wind</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 2% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 44% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_33"><h3>Unbroken</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Rapid Recovery</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 2% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 66% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 124</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_not_yet" data-title="Not Yet"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Not Yet</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_NOT_YET"><h3>Not Yet</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Adds +1 to the personal-life cap (normally 4 to 5). Acquiring Not Yet raises the maximum only; it does not award a life. Extra-life pickups fill the current personal cap before overflow can revive a teammate.</p><p class="actors">Cooperative Heroes with personal lives</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 125</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_poison_proc" data-title="Venomous"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Venomous</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_1"><h3>Venomous</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Your hit has a 55% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_2"><h3>Toxic</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Venomous</p><p>Your hit has a 75% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_3"><h3>Virulent</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Toxic</p><p>Your hit has a 95% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 126</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_burst_size" data-title="Extra Round"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Extra Round</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_1"><h3>Extra Round</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Add 1 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_2"><h3>Extended Volley</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Extra Round</p><p>Add 2 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_3"><h3>Full Barrage</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Extended Volley</p><p>Add 3 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 127</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_clumsy_proc" data-title="Distracting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Distracting</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_1"><h3>Distracting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your hit has a 55% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_2"><h3>Disorienting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Distracting</p><p>Your hit has a 75% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_3"><h3>Discombobulating</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Disorienting</p><p>Your hit has a 95% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 128</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_exploding_damage_dice" data-title="Perfect Ten"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Perfect Ten</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D10"><h3>Perfect Ten</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your ordinary d10 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 10 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d10 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D8"><h3>Eight Is Enough</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Perfect Ten</p><p>Your ordinary d8 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 8 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d8 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D4"><h3>Fourtunate</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Eight Is Enough</p><p>Your ordinary d4 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 4 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d4 damage rolls</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 129</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_immolate_proc" data-title="Singeing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Singeing</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_1"><h3>Singeing</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your hit has a 55% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_2"><h3>Scorching</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Singeing</p><p>Your hit has a 75% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_3"><h3>Incendiary</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Scorching</p><p>Your hit has a 95% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 130</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_magnum_deadeye" data-title="Deadeye"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Deadeye</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_MAGNUM_DEADEYE"><h3>Deadeye</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Stand perfectly still for 0.5 seconds to empower your next primary attack: double damage with a standard weapon, or triple damage with the .357 Magnum. One attack consumes the aim.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled actors using a standard player weapon</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 131</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_rate_of_fire" data-title="Hair Trigger"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hair Trigger</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_1"><h3>Hair Trigger</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Increase firearm firing rate by 55%.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 132</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_reload_cadence" data-title="Quick Reload"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Quick Reload</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD"><h3>Quick Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Reduce ordinary weapon reload time by 66%. This does not shorten SMG cooling or attack windups.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 133</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_shrink" data-title="Little Guy"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Little Guy</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SHRINK"><h3>Little Guy</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Your visible body becomes 30% smaller. Your movement hull, weapon traces and interaction reach stay the same. Incompatible with Big Guy.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 134</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_smg_heat" data-title="Heat Sink"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Heat Sink</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_HEAT_SINK"><h3>Heat Sink</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Each SMG round has a 66% chance to add no heat. Overheat threshold: 8. Overheating still locks firing for 2 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 135</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_spring_heel" data-title="Spring Heel"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Spring Heel</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SPRING_HEEL"><h3>Spring Heel</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Triples the otherwise-current apex height of every voluntary jump, including ordinary jump, Wall Jump and Cloud Step, using sqrt(3) times vertical takeoff impulse. While legitimately airborne, voluntary horizontal movement and air control are 1.5x normal, without amplifying discrete kicks, authored Cloud Step impulses, BaseVelocity or conveyors. Push, knockback, falls, scripted relocation, ladders, stairs, and other non-jump movement are unchanged; anti-top, gate, ceiling, and progression blockers remain authoritative.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 136</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_strafe" data-title="Strafer"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Strafer</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_STRAFER_1"><h3>Strafer</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Voluntary left/right strafing is 75% faster. Only the lateral component changes; Rogue and other ordinary movement bonuses compose. Forced movement, ladders and knockback are unchanged.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 137</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_wall_jump" data-title="Wall Jump"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Wall Jump</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_WALL_JUMP"><h3>Wall Jump</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Press Jump within 24 units of a vertical wall to jump and kick away. Four uses before landing; no Magic cost. Spring Heel increases the jump height.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 138</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_ammo_regeneration_floor" data-title="Field Supply"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Field Supply</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_44"><h3>Field Supply</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13</p><p>Owned regenerative firearm ammunition refills to 44% of family capacity, rounded up, with 22% faster per-round recovery. No-fire delay and capacity stay unchanged; no instant ammo, Wand charges, consumables or AR2 secondary ammo.</p><p class="acto]====]
